{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560407-ventrue-back-to-nature-bloodline","id":560407,"title":"Ventrue \"back to nature\" Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-18T22:22:02-07:00","id":560407,"title":"Ventrue \"back to nature\" Bloodline","content":"So VtR has a lot of really interesting hints that the Gangrel and Ventrue come from a common ancestor, so I was thinking- could that be a possible inspiration for a Bloodline? A rural, nature-focused Ventrue Bloodline that regains access to Protean (assuming the clan once had it)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T23:16:32-07:00","id":560450,"title":"","content":"It might be cool to make a Bloodline with Animalism, Dominate, Protean, and Resilience that Gangrel and Ventrue could join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-19-2015, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:04:19-07:00","id":560649,"title":"","content":"I'd also include bits about an alternative view. How this isn't a throwback so much as its an evolution. The clans, through feeding, are eventually merging into one uber-clan. A vampy singularity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:38:20-07:00","id":560747,"title":"","content":"That's sort of where I sometimes like to put Tzimisce: Gangrel who lord it over man, beast and the land. The Ventrue ones gained fine control over the minds of their subjects at the expense of control over the shape of their own bodies (and that of their ghouls with a series of fancy protean devotions) . I find a Ventrue to Gangrel bloodline more difficult to picture, but that could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:41:42-07:00","id":560752,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce sounds about right from what I remember. However if not, that would be a fun one to play. COMMAND ALL THE THINGS!<br /> <br /> =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:43:45-07:00","id":560754,"title":"","content":"Dominate+Protean = Vissictitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:17:23-07:00","id":560790,"title":"","content":"Not so much, just that I get the vibe of Tzimisce from a Gangrel/Ventrue mix. The ability to control all. Not quite sure where the flesh crafting would come in though. Maybe some mad scientist discovered it with all of his 'subjects'. Crossing animals with humans and what not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:29:51-07:00","id":560796,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude could be a Bloodline Gift, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:03:26-07:00","id":560847,"title":"","content":"That it could. Which is why I mentioned the scientist. Maybe he created the bloodline/founded Vicissitude. (I actually think I read something somewhere about a scientist who either did that, or something similar). There's one or two conversions for it in the homebrew thread isn't there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:08:12-07:00","id":560853,"title":"","content":"Edit: Yes, yes there are two conversions in the homebrew thread =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:17:25-07:00","id":560951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560407-ventrue-back-to-nature-bloodline?p=560790#post560790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much, just that I get the vibe of Tzimisce from a Gangrel/Ventrue mix. The ability to control all. Not quite sure where the flesh crafting would come in though. Maybe some mad scientist discovered it with all of his 'subjects'. Crossing animals with humans and what not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I based my Tzimisce around Ahzi Dahaka i.e. the aspiration to make the world part of oneself. In <i>Blood and Smoke</i>, Seeker Parson describes ghouls as extensions of their regnant like extra limbs. My idea was that Tzimisce are able to extend their protean abilities to their ghouls to create szlachta and then leave them in that state. No living chaise longues or wallskin, but &quot;hellhounds&quot; are fine and they don't necessarily have to be born as dogs or wolves.<br /> <br /> So for these guys, &quot;Your body is mine to shape as I see fit&quot;, whereas for those who can use dominate &quot;Your mind is mine to shape as I see fit&quot;. Auspex is good for that sort thing too. The reason they're known for sleeping near their native soil is connected to their need to sleep in the soil in order to reshape ghouls in different ways. And then Lord of the Land would be the main reason for their hospitality traditions. Aside from that, it doesn't take much to tick off transhumanist Gangrel at the best of times. Etiquette a l'Invictus would be essential to prevent visiting elders from ripping each other to shreds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:10:25-07:00","id":561069,"title":"","content":"I wrote a version of the Tzimisce with a similar theme in mind to what Spencer from the Hills is suggesting, though I ditched them actually having Protean because I felt that the Vicissitude would be more like Dominating the Flesh or something like that.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in revising it further to simplify the mechanics of Vicissitude, but I haven't gotten around to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:09:58-07:00","id":561199,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Ya I can see them not having Protean. Animalism + Dominate to control your test subjects. Just more of Protean for ones self. Sadly, I never got to play much with Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:52:14-07:00","id":561226,"title":"","content":"Ah, I was thinking more of a fire-lit &quot;Invictus&quot; with spiritual ambitions that existed at the same time as the Camarilla than scientists. It was also my intention to have Gangrel who learnt how to become tyrants without dominate, majesty or even nightmare. When I play with Masquerade clan concepts for Requiem, I first look at how they'd exist before the 15th century and what their relationship with the Camarilla was if any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}